# Vocabulary lookup uses only free, offline-friendly sources (bundled WordNet + the community
# Free Dictionary API + CC-CEDICT) and needs NO API keys. This file documents the optional
# server settings; copy it to .env only if you want to override a default.

# HOST=127.0.0.1
# PORT=3000
# LOG_LEVEL=info
# DATABASE_DIR=
# The `dev` script persists to a git-ignored .data/db by default; `start` is in-memory. Set
# DATABASE_DIR to a path to choose your own location, or "" to force in-memory under `dev`.
# SOURCE_FILES_DIR=./.data/sources
# IMAGE_RESOURCES_DIR=./.data/images
# Durable file roots kept for provenance: SOURCE_FILES_DIR holds uploaded source files, and
# IMAGE_RESOURCES_DIR holds extracted image resources. `pnpm data:backup` captures the database plus
# both of these roots into one verified archive; `pnpm data:restore` loads them into a fresh, empty
# target. See docs/BACKUP.md. Keep archives out of git.
# EPUB_UPLOAD_LIMIT_BYTES=52428800
# WEB_DIR=
# Single-origin deploy (see docs/DEPLOY.md): set WEB_DIR to the built web client
# (src/apps/web/dist) and the server also serves the app at `/` alongside `/api/*`. Unset in dev,
# where Vite serves the client separately.

# DIARY_TIDY_MODEL=llama3.1:8b
# EXPLAIN_MODEL=qwen2.5
# The two optional, local-only AI utilities — both off by default, so the base install is deterministic
# and needs no model. DIARY_TIDY_MODEL names the local Ollama model that lightly tidies a voice-diary
# transcript (filler/pause cleanup only, never rewording; unset = the raw transcript is kept verbatim).
# EXPLAIN_MODEL names the local model behind the lookup "AI 解释" contextual gloss for Chinese (unset =
# the tab shows its honest "unavailable" state). The easiest way to fill these in is `pnpm setup:ai`,
# which installs Ollama (with a Y/N prompt), pulls both models, and writes DIARY_TIDY_MODEL +
# EXPLAIN_MODEL here. Nothing is sent to a cloud provider. One-release compatibility: if DIARY_TIDY_MODEL
# is unset, an existing local `COACH_MODEL` value is honored as a read-only alias for it; new config
# should use DIARY_TIDY_MODEL.

# LOCAL_ASR_BINARY=
# LOCAL_ASR_MODEL=
# Local speech-to-text for the voice diary (see docs/SPEECH.md). This provider-neutral pair is the stable
# boundary: LOCAL_ASR_BINARY is the local speech executable (it answers `--contract-version` and emits the
# JSON contract) and LOCAL_ASR_MODEL is its model identifier. Set BOTH to enable it, or neither to leave
# voice-diary capture transcribing to empty; setting exactly one is a startup configuration error. When
# this pair is set it is authoritative and any legacy WHISPER_* below is ignored (setup/doctor flag the
# leftover). `pnpm setup:voice` provisions the bundled Qwen3-ASR-1.7B provider into an isolated, Whetstone-
# owned virtual environment (under ignored `.data/`, never your global Python) and writes THIS pair,
# removing any legacy WHISPER_* below.

# WHISPER_BINARY=
# WHISPER_MODEL_PATH=
# Legacy local Whisper STT (see docs/SPEECH.md) - kept working only as a fallback while installations
# migrate to LOCAL_ASR_BINARY + LOCAL_ASR_MODEL above. Used only when NEITHER new key is present: both
# WHISPER_BINARY (the whisper CLI / wrapper launcher) and WHISPER_MODEL_PATH (a faster-whisper model size
# like `small`/`base.en`, or a path) must be set. Whisper always auto-detects the spoken language - there
# is no language override. Unset = voice-diary capture transcribes to empty. These legacy keys are honored
# only as a manual fallback; `pnpm setup:voice` now installs the Qwen3-ASR default above and no longer
# writes them.
